---
# Scheduling priority for the two workload classes a cluster has to separate.
# Without them everything runs at priority 0 and a CI burst competes with
# platform workloads on nothing but arrival order — and the alert that would
# catch it (KubeCPUOvercommit) excludes the CI namespaces by design.
#
# Two classes, not a ladder: system-cluster-critical / system-node-critical
# already cover the pieces whose loss takes the cluster with them (kube-vip,
# CoreDNS, metrics-server, the tailnet DNS proxy), and inventing tiers between
# them adds preemption paths nobody reasons about.
#
# `platform` is APPLIED per workload, via the `priorityClassName` value of each
# platform HelmRelease. Deliberately NOT applied to metrics-server or kured:
# both already carry a HIGHER built-in class, so setting this would be a
# downgrade. App tenants and CI job pods keep their own classes.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS IN sources/ AND NOT configs/: the Priority admission plugin
# rejects a pod naming a PriorityClass that does not exist. The controllers
# stage creates such pods and runs BEFORE configs, and it is `wait: true` — so a
# class defined in configs would never be reached on a cold bootstrap. sources
# is the one stage everything else dependsOn.
apiVersion: scheduling.k8s.io/v1
kind: PriorityClass
metadata:
  name: platform
value: 100000
globalDefault: false
preemptionPolicy: PreemptLowerPriority
description: >-
  Platform workloads that must win scheduling against ordinary apps and CI job
  pods. Applied per workload — nothing inherits it.
{%- if git_backend == 'gitlab_selfhosted' %}

---
# The load-bearing half: every unclassed pod sits at 0 and therefore outranks a
# CI job pod without any of them needing a class. preemptionPolicy Never means a
# CI pod waits for room instead of evicting anything — CI should queue, never
# displace.
#
# THE GATING RULE for `git_backend`, stated once here because this is the first
# object in the tree that uses it: gate only what a non-GitLab forge would leave
# with no consumer at all. This class is set exclusively by the two runner
# modules, which are gated on the same answer, so an ungated copy would be a
# class nothing names. A module that merely DEFAULTS to a git_host-derived value
# (registry-cache) is not gated — its upstream is an edit-here knob, not a forge
# dependency. `git_backend: github` is validator-blocked today, so every such
# gate is forward-compat scaffolding rather than a live switch.
apiVersion: scheduling.k8s.io/v1
kind: PriorityClass
metadata:
  name: ci-jobs
value: -10
globalDefault: false
preemptionPolicy: Never
description: >-
  GitLab CI job pods. Ranked below every unclassed workload and never preempts —
  a burst queues rather than displacing running workloads. Set via
  [runners.kubernetes] priority_class_name in the runner TOMLs.
{%- endif %}
